\details{
DefiLlama is a \strong{keyless} public JSON API, so this base overrides just the
envelope seam and leaves authentication as connectcore's no-auth default:
\itemize{
\item \code{.parse_envelope()} — the DefiLlama error/empty-body envelope (via the internal
\code{parse_defillama_response()}): it raises a typed \link{defillama_conditions} error on
a non-2xx status, treats an empty 2xx body as "no data" (\code{NULL}, which each
parser turns into a typed zero-row table), and otherwise parses the JSON.
}
\subsection{Sync vs async}{

The \code{async} argument selects the execution mode for every method:
\itemize{
\item \code{async = FALSE} (default): methods return a \link[data.table:data.table]{data.table::data.table}.
\item \code{async = TRUE}: methods return a \link[promises:promise]{promises::promise} that resolves to the same
\code{data.table}.
}

The mode is stored once as \code{private$.is_async} and threaded through every method's
\code{connectcore::then_or_now(res, ..., is_async = private$.is_async)} tail; nothing
hardcodes it. Consume promises with \code{\link[coro:async]{coro::async()}} and \code{await()}; drive the loop
in a script with \code{while (!later::loop_empty()) later::run_now()}.
}

\subsection{Hosts}{

DefiLlama splits its surface across two hosts: the main host
(\code{\link[=defillama_base_url]{defillama_base_url()}}, \verb{https://api.llama.fi}) serves protocols, TVL, DEX
volumes, and fees; the stablecoins host (\code{\link[=defillama_stablecoins_url]{defillama_stablecoins_url()}},
\verb{https://stablecoins.llama.fi}) serves the stablecoins domain. Each subclass sets
the correct host as its \code{base_url} default, so a client only ever speaks to one
host.
}

\subsection{Retries}{

\code{max_tries > 1} opts every request (all are idempotent GETs) into automatic retry
on a transient failure (HTTP 408/429/5xx or a dropped connection) with jittered
backoff, delegated to \code{\link[connectcore:build_request]{connectcore::build_request()}}. DefiLlama's public endpoints
are read-only, so retrying is always safe. Default \code{3} (a modest retry budget for
a free public feed).

